{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC6 satisfied — post-merge patchset run observed with a passing scanner-integration job\n\nAC6 required, in its own words, that **after Stage A lands**, a *subsequent* real Gerrit patchset run\nshow the Verified workflow containing a `scanner-integration` job that executes and passes. That\nevidence now exists.\n\n```\nStage A merged (ea08483d825e)      2026-09-06 00:47:30Z\nrun 34005589010                    created 2026-09-06 02:05:59Z   <-- AFTER the merge\n  workflow: change 2704 patchset 1 (rev f322057eba43...)\n  jobs: 21\n  scanner-integration (pinned Semgrep + Gitleaks on the patchset)\n      status:     completed\n      conclusion: success\n      job id:     101412298454\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/34005589010\n\n### Why this run and not the earlier one\n\nThe previously-recorded run `33999972271` is CL 2701's **own pre-merge** run and does not satisfy an\nAC whose text begins \"After Stage A lands\". The nearest candidate after that, run `34001920346`\n(change 2703 patchset 1), was created at 00:40:46Z — **6 minutes 44 seconds before** the merge — and\nits 21 jobs contain no `scanner-integration` at all, which is itself confirmation that the job only\nappears once Stage A is on `main` (the workflow is dispatched from `main`). Run 34005589010 is the\nfirst patchset run created after the merge, and it has the job.\n\nThat sequence is worth keeping on the record: the job's *absence* at 00:40 and *presence* at 02:05,\nacross the 00:47 merge, is stronger evidence than the passing run alone. It shows the mechanism took\neffect at the merge rather than having been there all along.\n\n### Scope note\n\nThis discharges the advisory stage only. Promotion to Verified voting is Stage B, tracked separately\nas `d645-8f51-0ff9-4070`, whose Gerrit change (2682) is currently `Verified -1` and in WIP under\nrepair. The graph already encodes the ordering — d645 shows `blocked by: 283b-7104-87c1-4015` — so\nthat dependency resolves with this ticket's close and does not need to be re-stated."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788661231107348001,"uuid":"8482974f-b41e-45b4-944d-cfcf1ad4b7f3"}